From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <rainb@tfwno.gf>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:27:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Port fsearch to Windows using the MSYS2 toolchain

Rebase of the win32compat branch (c3b0b25, f8fcac5) onto upstream master.

- win32_compat.[ch] provides the POSIX pieces the core needs on Windows
  (flock, lstat, fnmatch, strptime, strcasestr, memrchr, dirent) with
  UTF-16 file APIs, and is built only for Windows hosts.
- The database scanner stats the full path on Windows, since there are no
  directory file descriptors there.
- GDesktopAppInfo and .desktop launchers are freedesktop-only; "Open with"
  looks the application up among the registered GIO apps instead.
- Parent folders open in Explorer with the file selected by default.
- test_query builds path needles with the platform separator, and skips
  the Turkic case mapping test on Windows, where GLib follows the thread
  locale instead of setlocale().
